Ownership enforcement mechanism
•	The BankingService implementation enforces ownership by:
•	Obtaining authenticated CustomerId exclusively via ICurrentUserAccessor.GetCurrentCustomerIdAsync() (which uses the server-side session cookie and session store).
•	All read queries filter by CustomerId == authenticatedCustomerId when selecting accounts, loans, credit cards, etc.
•	The controller additionally checks ICurrentUserAccessor for presence and returns 401 if unauthenticated; however the service is the ultimate authority for ownership (defense in depth).
How authenticated CustomerId is obtained
•	CurrentUserService reads the NB_SID HttpOnly secure cookie, hashes it, and looks up CustomerSession where TokenHash matches and session is not revoked and not expired. It exposes GetCurrentCustomerIdAsync() which returns the server-side CustomerId derived from the session. The application services use the application-level ICurrentUserAccessor (mapped to CurrentUserService) to retrieve the authenticated customer id.
